{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"How the default placeholders’ built-in text is localized, how to add a language, and how to show different text instead without touching ScreenStates itself.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/localization"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default Empty\/Loading\/Error placeholders’ text — “Nothing Here,” “Loading,” “Retry,” “Something Went Wrong,” “Connection Issue” — comes from a String Catalog, "},{"code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", resolved from ScreenStates’ own bundle ("},{"code":"Bundle.module","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") rather than your app’s. That’s deliberate: a custom title your app passes in (see below) is never run back through localization, and a language you add to "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"your own"}]},{"type":"text","text":" app’s catalog has no effect on these five strings — they only ever resolve against ScreenStates’ bundle. English, Spanish, French, and Russian are built in today."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Adding a language to ScreenStates","level":2,"anchor":"Adding-a-language-to-ScreenStates","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is a change to the package itself, not something a consuming app can do on its own — it needs a PR. Open "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings"},{"type":"text","text":" and add a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localizations"},{"type":"text","text":" entry for the new language code under each of the five string keys:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"json","code":["\"Retry\" : {","  \"comment\" : \"Title of the button that retries loading after an error.\",","  \"localizations\" : {","    \"en\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Retry\" } },","    \"de\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Wiederholen\" } }","  }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every one of the five keys needs an entry for every language — a string present in English but missing a translation elsewhere fails CI (see below). "},{"code":"ScreenStatesStrings.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s doc comments list all five keys and their English text if you’re starting from scratch."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Overriding text per-app","level":2,"anchor":"Overriding-text-per-app","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You don’t need a new language, or a PR, to show different text than the built-in default — two options, depending on how much you want to replace:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" takes a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"title"},{"type":"text","text":" directly, bypassing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Localizable.xcstrings"},{"type":"text","text":" entirely for that one string. Pass your own localized string (from your own app’s String Catalog, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSLocalizedString"},{"type":"text","text":", whatever) instead of the default:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title: String(localized: \"No Results\"))"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has no equivalent for its title or Retry button text today — only the error’s own message is customizable, via ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For anything else — the Error placeholder’s title, the Retry button’s text, or any text at all in a shape the built-in views don’t expose a parameter for — pass a fully custom placeholder instead of the default one, via "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"empty"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loading"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error"},{"type":"text","text":" builder closures (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") or "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateViewController","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"‘s equivalent. A custom placeholder can still reuse "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" so VoiceOver announces transitions with the same wording your custom text uses, instead of the default’s."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Localization"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Localization","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateView":{"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstateview","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateView"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","title":"ScreenStateView","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateView"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Renders the right content for a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", switching between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Empty \/ Loading \/ Data \/ Error automatically."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"ScreenStates","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates","abstract":[{"text":"Give any screen a standard ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Empty"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Loading"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Error"},{"type":"text","text":" state, usable from both UIKit and SwiftUI."}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI":{"kind":"article","role":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Drive a SwiftUI screen’s four states with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","title":"Getting Started with SwiftUI","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/gettingstartedwithswiftui"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateContainerView":{"title":"ScreenStateContainerView","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"code":"UIView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that swaps its content for the right placeholder based on a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState"},{"text":", mirroring ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView"},{"text":" from the SwiftUI side.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateContainerView"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateContainerView"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatecontainerview"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenState/accessibilityAnnouncement":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"accessibilityAnnouncement","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"title":"accessibilityAnnouncement","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The same text the default placeholders announce to VoiceOver for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this case, reusable by a fully custom placeholder that wants to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"announce transitions with the same wording instead of inventing its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":", since at that point a custom placeholder’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own content is what VoiceOver should read, not a transition"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"announcement."}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstate\/accessibilityannouncement"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateDisplayableError":{"abstract":[{"text":"Lets an error type supply its own user-facing message, distinct from","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"localizedDescription","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — which is often a debugging string (or, for a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plain ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Error"},{"type":"text","text":" with no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomStringConvertible"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocalizedError"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conformance, just the type name) rather than something to put in front"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the person using the app."}],"title":"ScreenStateDisplayableError","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateDisplayableError"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateDisplayableError"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatedisplayableerror","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenState":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The four canonical states of a screen: nothing to show yet, in flight,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"showing data, or failed."}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstate","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenState"}],"title":"ScreenState","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenState"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/GettingStartedWithUIKit":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Getting Started with UIKit","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/gettingstartedwithuikit","abstract":[{"text":"Drive a UIKit screen’s four states with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/Accessibility":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything the default placeholders — and your own custom ones — get for free: VoiceOver, Reduce Motion, Increase Contrast, Dynamic Type, and stable identifiers for XCUITest."}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/accessibility","type":"topic","title":"Accessibility"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateViewController":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstateviewcontroller","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateViewController","title":"ScreenStateViewController","abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"code":"UIViewController","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" base class that owns a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pinned to the view’s edges and bound to a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wrapping the boilerplate every UIKit screen using ScreenStates","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"otherwise repeats in ","type":"text"},{"code":"viewDidLoad()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateViewController"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateViewController"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore":{"title":"ScreenStateStore","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holder of a screen’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState"},{"text":", driving both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftUI and UIKit consumers from a single source of truth.","